{
  "title": "Global soil fungi: R workflow for global maps of soil fungal diversity, ectomycorrhizal structure and taxonomic resolution at 250 m",
  "description": "R and Google Earth Engine code supporting the article: Moquedace, C.M.; Baldi, C.G.O.; Gomes, L.C.; Siqueira, R.G.; Xue, P.; Minasny, B.; Schaefer, C.E.G.R.; Francelino, M.R.; Cerri, C.E.P.; Poppiel, R.R.; Pelegrino, M.H.P.; Soares, L.U.L.; Dematt\u00ea, J.A.M.; Fernandes-Filho, E.I. Soil fungal diversity is greatest where taxonomic knowledge is poorest, not where ectomycorrhizal lineages are richest. Manuscript under review; the reference will be added on publication. The workflow builds a 146-layer covariate stack at 250 m (Equal Earth), derives six fungal community dimensions from GloSED, fits quantile random forest models with spatial block validation, predicts the median, standard deviation and 5, 25, 75 and 95% quantiles in every cell, and prepares the figures, tables and distribution copies (Zenodo and Google Earth Engine).",
